<title>UK: ICO coffee exports down at 6.34 mln bags in Dec.</title>
<headline>ICO coffee exports down at 6.34 mln bags in Dec.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Coffee Organisation (ICO) exporting members exports fell to 6.34 million 60-kg bags in December from 6.78 million in November but up from 6.25 million in December 1995, ICO figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>In the 12 months to December 1996 total exports rose to 74.54 million bags from 67.00 million in the same 1995 period.</p>
<p>In the first three months of the current 1996/97 coffee year to December total exports were up at 18.84 million from 17.51 million in the same 1995/96 period.</p>
<p>Latest ICO export data, in thousand bags, included --</p>
<p>		     Dec 96    Dec  95     Oct/Dec 96     Oct/Dec 95</p>
<p>    Brazil	 1,769     1,061	 5,750	    3,238</p>
<p>    Colombia     1,041     1,194	 3,301	    3,337</p>
<p>    Guatemala	443	 305	   979		680</p>
<p>    Mexico	   390	 421	   874		820</p>
<p>    Indonesia	264	 365	 1,006	    1,404</p>
<p>    Uganda	   514	 388	 1,291		850</p>
<p>    Vietnam	  439	 586	 1,075	    1,265</p>
<p>    Ivory Coast     38	 124	   196		409</p>
<p>-- Jalil Hamid, London newsroom +44 171 542 4985</p>
</text>
